SCRIPT='A single-narrator motivational essay: failed-budget hook; thesis that spending is an identity problem; cognitive dissonance and willpower-as-muscle; friend with rental properties; tiny actions as identity evidence; first $1,000/$10,000; old-identity resistance; language shift ("I don\'t spend money on this"); consistency over amount ($50 x 12 vs $600); walking-away money and confidence; habits over money; lottery winners; discomfort as grief; social pressure and boundaries; six-month habit; cortisol and scarcity; knowledge vs action; narrator\'s $50 index fund; rebuild-speed thought experiment; dark side of friendships; close on options. Few numerical claims. Contested or overgeneralised: ego-depletion willpower model, lottery winners go broke, $10,000 "rewrites brain chemistry". The stored text ends on a dangling word.'
